     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. The usual maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin, and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release in many labels. This order is about twice that. A dose that high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and severe GI toxicity, even with normal kidney function.\n\nHere are some possibilities, depending on what was intended:\n- **850 mg three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the usual max, and it may be what was meant if \"1700\" was a typo.\n- **1,700 mg/day in total.** This could be given as 850 mg twice daily.\n- **500 mg to 1,000 mg two or three times daily.** This is a common range, and it's usually titrated up gradually.\n\nPlease confirm the dose you want. If you do intend 1,700 mg three times daily, tell me the clinical reason and I'll enter it with a note documenting that it was verified."
      }
     ],
